# EVERY FILE HERE IS CONTENT-ADDRESSED, SO NOTHING MAY BE REWRITTEN.
#
# git's line-ending normalisation turned every CRLF in a published map into a
# LF, which changed the bytes, which broke the SHA-256 the index had already
# recorded - so a map downloaded fine, hashed differently, and was refused.
#
# "-text" tells git these are opaque bytes. It must stay that way for as long
# as maps are named by their hash, which is forever.
* -text
